# Latin: a son / salsa at ~190 on a 2-3 son clave, written for Polly over C M7. Drums by hand: the Groove MIDI
# Dataset's latin takes are kit grooves, and salsa needs the clave, congas, cowbell and timbales.
# Patterns are two bars, the length of the clave: bar 1 its 2 side, bar 2 its 3 side.
# Main A: claves, the conga tumbao (slap on 2, open tones on 4 and its and), maracas, the bass tumbao
# (the and of 2 and beat 4, anticipating), the piano montuno in two alternating voicings, soft strings.
# Main B: the cowbell on the beat, timbale accents, a crash, a trombone mambo riff, the strings up.
# Intro (4 bars, two claves): the piano montuno over the clave and maracas alone, then the congas, the bass
# tumbao and the strings join; a timbale pickup into Main A.
# Fill BA (1 bar): a band break on the clave's 2 side: everyone hits the one, the and of 2 and beat 4 (held)
# with timbales and a crash, the congas out.
style Latin
tempo 190

track d1 type=bypass chan=10 vol=100 rev=30
track d2 type=bypass chan=10 vol=100 rev=30   # shares channel 10 with d1: the same mixer
track pc type=bypass chan=10 vol=100 rev=30
track ba type=bass program=32 chan=2 lo=E1 hi=G3 hikey=F# vol=114 rev=16
track c1 type=chord1 program=0 chan=3 lo=G3 hi=G5 hikey=F# vol=92 pan=50 rev=40
